WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.436 --> 00:00:12.479
It almost time for cooking class.

2
00:00:13.559 --> 00:00:15.700
The kids were talking outside the kitchen door.

3
00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:20.621
"I wonder what we're cooking today," Nina said.

4
00:00:20.641 --> 00:00:24.742
"It can't be as good as what I ate last night!"

5
00:00:25.723 --> 00:00:27.083
Bobby patted his stomach.

6
00:00:28.843 --> 00:00:29.604
"What was that?"

7
00:00:29.984 --> 00:00:30.784
Jason asked.

8
00:00:32.653 --> 00:00:36.235
"My grandfather took me to a baseball game," Bobby said.

9
00:00:36.255 --> 00:00:41.379
"I ate two hot dogs, a hamburger, and some pepperoni pizza!"

10
00:00:44.941 --> 00:00:47.403
"Whoa! I could never eat all that!"

11
00:00:47.863 --> 00:00:48.523
Izzie said.

12
00:00:49.664 --> 00:00:51.325
Bobby made a muscle with his arm.

13
00:00:51.345 --> 00:00:55.008
"I'm growing, so I need to eat a lot."

14
00:01:00.456 --> 00:01:03.477
Inside, the kids washed their hands and put on their aprons.

15
00:01:03.497 --> 00:01:09.920
"This is one of my favorite vegetarian meals," Chef said.

16
00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:12.341
"Sesame noodles with tofu."

17
00:01:13.981 --> 00:01:15.222
Bobby looked surprised.

18
00:01:15.242 --> 00:01:18.243
"You're a vegetarian, Chef?"

19
00:01:19.904 --> 00:01:21.244
"No," Chef said.

20
00:01:21.264 --> 00:01:24.586
"But I eat meatless meals several times a week.

21
00:01:25.586 --> 00:01:27.087
This dish is quick and easy.

22
00:01:28.047 --> 00:01:29.928
But we have to prepare everything first."

23
00:01:32.241 --> 00:01:34.302
Izzie filled a pot with water for the noodles.

24
00:01:35.443 --> 00:01:37.544
She put it on the stove and turned on the heat.

25
00:01:40.646 --> 00:01:41.867
Jason made the sauce.

26
00:01:43.808 --> 00:01:47.550
He poured soy sauce, sesame oil, and rice vinegar into a bowl.

27
00:01:50.372 --> 00:01:53.294
Then he added ginger, garlic powder, and black pepper.

28
00:01:55.375 --> 00:01:56.836
He mixed everything together.

29
00:01:58.632 --> 00:02:02.094
Izzie chopped green onions, and Nina peeled and grated a carrot.

30
00:02:04.515 --> 00:02:06.876
Bobby drained the water from the tofu package.

31
00:02:06.896 --> 00:02:11.338
"Tofu falls apart easily," Chef said.

32
00:02:11.358 --> 00:02:13.619
"So treat it gently."

33
00:02:18.001 --> 00:02:20.322
Bobby carefully removed the block of tofu.

34
00:02:22.963 --> 00:02:25.784
He cut it into small cubes and sprinkled them with salt.

35
00:02:27.444 --> 00:02:31.186
"We made chocolate tofu pudding with Miss Shelly," he said.

36
00:02:31.206 --> 00:02:34.328
"But I don't know where tofu comes from."

37
00:02:34.348 --> 00:02:36.129
"I know!"

38
00:02:36.429 --> 00:02:37.109
Nina said.

39
00:02:37.129 --> 00:02:39.971
"It's made from soybeans."

40
00:02:42.152 --> 00:02:44.273
Chef poured some cooking oil into a pan.

41
00:02:45.494 --> 00:02:48.315
When it was hot, he stir-fried the cubes of tofu.

42
00:02:48.335 --> 00:02:53.278
"Eating plants is okay," Bobby said.

43
00:02:53.298 --> 00:02:56.980
"But at my house we eat meat every day.

44
00:02:57.928 --> 00:02:59.649
Meat helps you grow strong."

45
00:02:59.669 --> 00:03:04.613
"Yes, meat has lots of protein," Chef said.

46
00:03:04.633 --> 00:03:08.936
"But you can get protein from tofu, beans, and nuts too.

47
00:03:10.697 --> 00:03:11.077
Oh, good.

48
00:03:11.397 --> 00:03:12.898
Our tofu is golden brown.

49
00:03:14.119 --> 00:03:15.240
That means it's ready."

50
00:03:17.081 --> 00:03:18.302
Jason checked the water.

51
00:03:19.303 --> 00:03:20.423
The water was boiling.

52
00:03:21.424 --> 00:03:22.905
He put the noodles in to cook.

53
00:03:22.925 --> 00:03:27.028
"I read a book about being a vegetarian," he said.

54
00:03:28.072 --> 00:03:29.092
"It helps the planet."

55
00:03:30.853 --> 00:03:31.593
Chef nodded.

56
00:03:31.613 --> 00:03:35.054
"Cows and other livestock produce greenhouse gases.

57
00:03:36.094 --> 00:03:37.214
Those heat up the planet.

58
00:03:38.815 --> 00:03:41.036
And it takes a lot of land to raise animals."

59
00:03:42.756 --> 00:03:46.197
"But vegetables grow in fields too," Bobby said.

60
00:03:46.217 --> 00:03:50.058
"Farmers need land to grow crops, don't they?"

61
00:03:50.078 --> 00:03:53.339
"Of course," Izzie said.

62
00:03:53.359 --> 00:03:57.660
"But it takes a lot of land to raise animals."

63
00:03:59.488 --> 00:04:00.729
Bobby started laughing.

64
00:04:03.511 --> 00:04:07.514
"I think everyone wants me to be a vegetarian!"

65
00:04:09.115 --> 00:04:09.995
Nina shrugged.

66
00:04:10.016 --> 00:04:12.557
"You can eat different dishes.

67
00:04:13.838 --> 00:04:15.860
Some with meat and some without."

68
00:04:17.821 --> 00:04:18.942
Chef checked the noodles.

69
00:04:18.962 --> 00:04:20.763
"They're ready!"

70
00:04:22.584 --> 00:04:23.665
The kids got bowls.

71
00:04:25.466 --> 00:04:27.448
Chef gave everyone a helping of noodles.

72
00:04:29.628 --> 00:04:31.629
"Now you can add tofu and vegetables."

73
00:04:33.150 --> 00:04:35.392
The kids put some tofu on top of the noodles.

74
00:04:36.313 --> 00:04:38.474
Then they added the green onions and carrot.

75
00:04:39.775 --> 00:04:41.716
Finally they poured on some sauce.

76
00:04:45.879 --> 00:04:47.100
Bobby started eating.

77
00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:50.062
"The sauce is great!

78
00:04:51.262 --> 00:04:52.984
And the tofu is good too!"

79
00:04:53.004 --> 00:04:56.086
"As good as pepperoni pizza?"

80
00:04:56.406 --> 00:04:57.246
Jason asked.

81
00:04:58.467 --> 00:04:59.268
Bobby grinned.

82
00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:01.582
"They're both good."
